{"_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": ""}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "Object Diagram"}, {"type": "position", "content": 11}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 2}, {"type": "level", "content": "A2.2"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you use when you talk about object diagrams."}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Describe common activities at work to a visitor using short sentences in familiar spoken and written situations.  Give detailed information related to UML and common related topics."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Identifies the expressions and vocabulary necessary for the description of places of work and jobs in common written and spoken situations.  Describes common activities related to Software Programming through the use of appropriate expressions, grammar and vocabulary in written or spoken situations according to the abilities related to this level."}], "type": "objectives"}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "enpe7n4le02ob11re1img01.jpg"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Simple Tenses in Negative Form"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You use the <span class=\"strong\">simple tenses </span>(past, present and future) to talk about concrete actions."}, {"type": "example", "content": "I didn't understand why our boss insists we use the object diagram for this project. "}, {"type": "example", "content": "I think it won't work!"}, {"type": "example", "content": "I think he doesn't know that sometimes object diagrams can be extremely abstract, and I'm not sure the entire team will be able to use them properly!"}, {"type": "text", "content": "We use the <span class=\"strong\"> simple present </span> to talk about routines or repetitive actions and general truths. Follow this structure to make negative sentences using present simple:"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<div class=\"center_text\"> Subject + <b>don't/doesn't + verb (base form)</b> + complement.</div>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Example:"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"italic\"> Abstract notation <span class=\"strong\"> doesn't </span> make the tasks easy to complete. </span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "We can use the <span class=\"strong\"> simple past </span> to make reference to actions that happened in the past. Something that started at a certain point in the past and finished in the past too. To use the simple past, you should follow the next structure: "}, {"type": "text", "content": "<div class=\"center_text\"> Subject + <b>didn't + verb (base form)</b> + complement</div>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Example:"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"italic\"> In the past, UML <span class=\"strong\"> didn't </span> include so many kinds of diagrams. </span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "We use the<span class=\"strong\"> future simple </span> to talk about actions that can happen in the future. Take a look at the structure below to see how to make negative sentences."}, {"type": "text", "content": "<div class=\"center_text\"> Subject +<b> won't + verb (base form)</b> + complement</div>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Examples:"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"italic\"> Object diagrams <span class=\"strong\"> won't </span> be used for this project.</span>"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "Prepositions of Place"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "You can use <b>prepositions of place</b> to help you locate objects in the space."}, {"type": "example", "content": "Especially because we can use object diagrams to analyze objects in a more realistic point of view, as well as the way we see the relationships between one another."}, {"type": "example", "content": "The good thing is that our boss decided to put a little explanation next to each class to reduce confusions."}, {"type": "text", "content": "There are many prepositions to refer to places; however, these are some of the most common ones:"}, {"type": "table", "content": "{\"rows\":5,\"columns\":2,\"cells\":[\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Preposition\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Use\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Between\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"You can use it to talk about an object that is in the middle of something.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Next to\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"You use it to refer to objects that are on the right or left (very close) of another object.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Under\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"It is used to refer to an object that is below another one or a surface.\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"Above\\\"}\",\"{\\\"type\\\": \\\"text\\\", \\\"content\\\": \\\"When something is up or ahead another object.\\\"}\"],\"styles\":\" intro_table_border instruction_table_background\"}"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Examples:"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"italic\"> What do the boxes in <span class=\"strong\"> between </span> represent?<br/> I don't understand what you drew <span class=\"strong\"> under </span> the main box in this diagram. </span>"}, {"type": "example", "content": "If you look at the boxes he made under the title, you will see that using this diagram makes perfect sense."}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "insist "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to underline, outline or demand something"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "verb"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I didn't understand why our boss insists we use the object diagram for this project. I think it won't work!"}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe7n4le02ob11aud01"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "analyze "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to think about something thoroughly and to examine it"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "verb"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Especially because we can use object diagrams to analyze objects in a more realistic point of view."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe7n4le02ob11aud02"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "make sense "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to be clear; to be logical or understandable"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "expression"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: If you look at the boxes he made under the title, you will see that using this diagram makes perfect sense."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe7n4le02ob11aud03"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "abstract  "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "something that is not concrete or that doesn't have a defined shape or sense  "}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "adjective"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: I think he doesn't know that sometimes object diagrams can be extremely abstract, and I'm not sure the entire team will be able to use them properly!  "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe7n4le02ob11aud04"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "complexity "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "difficulty, intricacy or complication"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "noun"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: The thing is that this project needs to explain the complexity of the relationships in different classes."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe7n4le02ob11aud05"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "be familiar with"}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to know about something or to have some skill on a field."}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "expression"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: They seem to be very familiar with UML notation."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe7n4le02ob11aud06"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Look for information about other UML diagrams "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Write the new information in your notebook. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Share the new information with your teacher and classmates."}], "type": "takeaway_extension"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "I investigate about other UML diagrams"}, {"type": "text", "content": "I write information about UML diagrams "}, {"type": "text", "content": "I talk about UML diagrams"}], "type": "takeaway_assessment"}], "type": "sena", "labs": [{"stimuli": [{"template_override": 1, "type": "welcome", "_data": [], "contents": [{}], "id": 0}, {"template_override": 1, "contents": [{"value": {"images": [{"time": "100", "image": "enpe7n4le02ob11re2img01.jpg", "id": 0, "text": "<strong>Sally</strong>: I didn't understand why our boss insists we use the object diagram for this project. I think it won't work!<br/>\n<strong>Jack</strong>: Relax, Sally! I think I agree with him. Especially because we can use object diagrams to analyze objects in a more realistic point of view, as well as the way we see the relationships between one another. If you look at the boxes he made under the title, you will see that using this diagram makes perfect sense.<br/>\n<strong>Sally</strong>: That's the problem, I didn't see if he added them. Besides, I think he doesn't know that sometimes object diagrams can be extremely abstract, and I'm not sure the entire team will be able to use them properly!<br/>"}, {"time": "45500", "image": "enpe7n4le02ob11re2img02.jpg", "id": 1, "text": "<strong>Jack</strong>: The thing is that this project needs to explain the complexity of the relationships in different classes. As you can see in the diagram, there are many of them. The good thing is that our boss decided to put a little explanation next to each class to reduce confusions.<br/>\n<strong>Sally</strong>: He didn't mention that to me!<br/>\n<strong>Jack</strong>: You weren't paying attention. In fact, despite the apparent complexity of these diagrams, the notation is quite simple, but we may need to give some instructions to some of the newest workers, so perhaps this object diagram could become a communication or instance diagram.<br/>"}, {"time": "87000", "image": "enpe7n4le02ob11re2img03.jpg", "id": 2, "text": "<strong>Sally</strong>: I was worried about that because if we have to explain everything to them, we won't finish the project on time. <br/>\n<strong>Jack</strong>: I don't think you need to worry about that. They seem to be very familiar with UML notation. Besides, remember that the most important part of modeling is not the diagram, but the process of creating it, which guides us towards what we expect the system to be like.<br/>\n<strong>Sally</strong>: You're right, Jack!<br/>"}], "coverimg": "enpe7n4le02ob11re2img01.jpg", "audiosrc": "enpe7n4le02ob11re2aud01"}, "type": "slideshow"}], "type": "audio", "_data": [], "id": 1, "title": ""}], "exercises": [{"stimuli_ids": [0], "template_override": 1, "questions": [], "type": "WLC", "_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": "I can talk about the object diagram. "}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": "I can explain different features related to object diagram. "}, {"type": "Learning Outcomes", "content": "I can describe different features related to object diagram."}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": "In your opinion, what is the best diagram in UML?"}, {"type": "Free Header Item", "content": "Do you think that UML diagrams reflect what the software will really look like? Explain."}], "type": "instructions"}, {"contents": [{"type": "group_name", "content": "Welcome"}], "type": "group"}, {"type": "feedback", "cont